      "id": "RFV-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-rare-size-density",
      "title": "The probability of one short isotropic flag type",
      "statement": "For an ordered composition j of total positive rank J≤q, the probability of realizing that flag type is at most κⱼ≤exp(−JU/2). Its normalized size density has integral at most one. Normalizing the flag-unfolding estimate by the whole quotient volume supplies κⱼ.",
      "hypotheses": "Finite-unramified CM data and positive finite normalized quotient volume, uniform signature (p,q), n=p+q, 2q+2≤n, f≥1, log n≥15, q²≤n, log d≤exp(n), log f≤sqrt(n), and the indicated Hermitian volume comparisons.",
